  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef la_orthogonal_projection(A: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Orthogonal Projection Matrix** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef la_orthogonal_projection(A: list) -> list:\n    mat = np.array(A, dtype=np.float64)\n    P = mat @ np.linalg.inv(mat.T @ mat) @ mat.T\n    return np.round(P, 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
